  "question": "Can a section header supply `historical` without becoming a prior?",
  "split": "held_out",
  "what_makes_it_a_cue_not_a_prior": "the defeater. A span whose own sentence says now/new/acute/current keeps its own framing and the header does not override it. A prior would apply regardless, which is the thing this package's span-level rule rejects.",
  "why": "21 of 32 held-out historical misses have no cue anywhere in the span's sentence. The dimension's bottleneck is vocabulary and no scope change can reach them.",
  "why_past_and_not_history": "on development, `Past Medical History` is 22/22 historical and `History of Present Illness` is 10/71. A rule keying on `history` fires on the HPI, whose header contains the word by grammatical accident while its content is the CURRENT admission. The naive arm is measured rather than dismissed."
